    "created_at": "2026-02-01T18:23:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-01T18:23:21Z",
    "body": "> I don't think that's correct necessarily. At least some of the callers do identify a _url_ that maybe needs to be passed along. It is kinda strange that Resource Timing expects this to be a string though, but presumably a parsed and then serialized string? It would be better if it took a URL.\n\nThis particular call is the resource timing fallback.it is invoked only the case where the actual resource timing wasn't marked for the iframe (cross origin no-TAO), so we mark the load event time together with the known URL of the frame (essentially a parsed URL representing the src attribute) as a \"response end\". \n\nGranted, I need to get a few of the details sorted for the PR but that's the big picture of this feature.",
